---
import { site } from '../../site.config';
---
<section id="vllm">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>vLLM</h2>
    <p>
      I'm a maintainer of <a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm">vLLM</a>, where I focus on
      efficient and portable execution of the model forward pass:
      <code>torch.compile</code> integration, fusion passes, kernels, and CUDA graphs.
      I am a code owner for the compilation infrastructure, as well as hardware-agnostic model
      definitions and related portability abstractions.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <b>Need a PR reviewed?</b> See instructions <a href="https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing/">here</a>.
        If the PR explicitly touches one of the areas mentioned above, you can DM me on vLLM Slack.
        Please include a short description of the PR and justification why you want me to review it.
        NB: I don't check GitHub mentions for the vllm repo (20+ notifications a day).
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="quiet">
      If you're looking for advice on vLLM deployment and performance, I also offer consultations.
      Please email me for more information.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
